Z||000007||ole_man||12-07-2001||09:55 AM||||If I recall correctly, the engine on the Sunbird faced the passenger side and the starter was in the back (facing the rear of the car). The Duke also faces the passenger side and the starter faces the front of the car. So the starter is in the wrong position for this swap. Are there any adapters available?||||reg||1
Z||000008||WKDFIRO||12-07-2001||10:33 AM||||Do a search on Delta 204T, there was a thread about it a while ago.||||reg||2
Z||000009||Eric_PA||12-08-2001||01:27 PM||||Well just went to the garage and took a few pics... I had no idea that the bolt pattern was different with this engine too. I am now wondering what GM tran's work with this engine. Maybe it's the same as the QUAD 4 but the sunbird OHC engines definately won't bolt to the fiero trans.<P>The top two bolt holes on the sunbird are 5 inches appart, the two top ones on the TH125 fiero trans are 5.25 inches appart.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dec08$01.jpg"> <BR>Here are the individual pics, first of 2.0 OHC sunbird engine, the other of the TH125 fiero trans. Notice how different they are.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dec08$02.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dec08$03.jpg"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Mach10||12-08-2001||03:20 PM||||Easy... Snake the trans from the Sunbird, too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000011||Raydar||12-08-2001||10:26 PM||||Was the Sunbird FWD? Or was it the one based on the Monza RWD configuration. If it's the Monza clone, that's the B-O-P bolt pattern. Actually, I've never seen a GM bolt pattern that looked like that. Might it be an Isuzu or Opel manufactured engine and tranny? I've never seen a FWD tranny with that bolt pattern. Which doesn't mean it doesn't exist, but if so, it's very uncommon.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Raydar||12-08-2001||10:29 PM|||| DOH!<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Eric_PA||12-09-2001||07:53 AM||||Raydar... it's from a FWD car and now that you mentioned the opel thing, I beleive it may be. This engine was manufactured in Brazil, and from my experience they don't last long (bad cams and head gaskets blow often). I have been throug 5 of these allready. I learned the hard way a few years ago when I went to swap one over to a five speed. I pulled the engine and then found out that the 5 speed did not match up. <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Gerald||12-09-2001||12:10 PM||||From the looks of that pic im willing to bet that changing the position of the starter is more troble then its worth. I was thinking about trying to find a 2l turbo to swap into my fiero but now if I want to do that I need the tranny too. Kinda like a quad 4 swap.||||reg||1
